    verification stopSaysNothingAboutDecisionsReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "3f3cfd40-8de8-4872-beaa-cbf992ba1f0c"; :>> title = "Sprint 589 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-06"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "THREE PASSES. (1) IS ANYTHING LEFT THAT ONLY EXISTED FOR THE LINE: yes, two things, and both are now deleted - the console-parity count and its test. (2) DOES THE REPLACEMENT HAVE A CONTROL: no, and it is stated as a residual in the skill and in the Decision rather than implied - no gate reads conversational output, so what keeps this honest is that the assessment is one command anyone can re-run against the published page. (3) DOES ANY DOC STILL DESCRIBE THE OLD BEHAVIOUR: CLAUDE.md did; corrected in the same commit."; }
    // RAN: keel suite . = 562 passed 0 failed (receipt 95df485b038f)
