    verification stopSaysNothingAboutDecisionsCloseOutGate : Test { :>> id = "2f082f89-d671-4e6c-b78c-fd2b89aed48d"; :>> title = "Sprint 589 closeOut gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-06"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "CLOSED. A green turn ends silent, and what waits on the human is computable by anyone who asks and published when it changes."; }
    // RAN: keel suite . = 562 passed 0 failed (receipt 95df485b038f)
    part stopSaysNothingAboutDecisionsCloseOutGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "f0ee47c1-dc8d-4468-9c76-5b047a4b0c22"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "HEAD"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-06"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus5"; }
    verification stopSaysNothingAboutDecisionsRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "0e6a018a-702f-4289-ab2a-c5cac1d2a5be"; :>> title = "Sprint 589 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-06"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN HELD. The avoidable one: a test asserted the literal source text of the branch it was policing, so deleting the branch broke it - and its own doc comment described exactly that failure mode, having been written when its PREDECESSOR broke the same way. Twice now, in the same file, for the same reason. NEW ITEM dcTestsBindToPropertiesNotSource (issue388). I first wrote here that no guard was possible because a test that greps its own source cannot be forbidden mechanically. That was wrong and the retro-backlog guard is what made me look again: a test that reads program source with include_str! and asserts on substrings of it is perfectly detectable. What is genuinely undecided is the TIER, since several checks here read files on purpose - the doc-claim, guard-catalogue and CLI-surface tests - so a blanket refusal would break legitimate controls; that choice is the substance of the item rather than an excuse for not raising it. The unavoidable one: nothing forces a post-analysis to run, which is a residual of the channel and not a defect of this change."; }
    // RAN: keel suite . = 562 passed 0 failed (receipt 95df485b038f)
